<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treasury of Minyas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a> · Also known as Tomb of Minyas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-khazneh">The Treasury</a> of Minyas is a Mycenaean tholos tomb at Orchomenos in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, named after the legendary king Minyas. Dating from the 13th century BCE, it is one of the largest tholos tombs in Greece, comparable to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treasury-of-atreus">Treasury of Atreus</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mycenae">Mycenae</a>. Its side chamber has a stone ceiling carved with spirals and rosettes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-schliemann">Heinrich Schliemann</a> excavated it in the 1880s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treasury-of-minyas.jpg" alt="Treasury of Minyas" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George E. Koronaios · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_derelict_state_of_the_tower_on_the_top_of_the_Acropolis_of_Orchomenus_on_September_30,_2020.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
